{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Summary\n\n`resolve_project` (`src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/projects_store.py`) collapses the\ntri-state `bridge_project` field's **`None` \"absent/legacy\" sentinel** into the same branch as\nthe explicit `\"\"` \"never-sync\" value, so a legacy ticket (no `bridge_project` flag) is\n**suppressed from outbound create** instead of routing to `legacy_default`. This is the direct\ncause of live DC rehearsal scenario 4 (`test_absent_project_resolves_to_legacy_default`) failing\nwith `assert 0 == 1` — the legacy-default ticket never lands in the legacy project.\n\n## Proven root cause (rebar-debug Phase 1 complete)\n\n`create_ticket` with no `bridge_project` stores `bridge_project: None` (present-but-null, seeded\nby the reducer `_state.py:58`), NOT an absent key. `resolve_project`'s `if not value: return None`\nlumps that `None` absent/legacy sentinel with `\"\"` never-sync, and its\n`if \"bridge_project\" not in ticket` branch is dead because the reducer ALWAYS materializes the\nkey — so `legacy_default` never fires for the cohort it exists to serve.\n\nThe authoritative **cef7 tri-state contract** (`src/rebar/reducer/_state.py:53-58`) states\n`bridge_project` is seeded `None` as the deliberate \"absent/legacy\" sentinel; `\"\"` is explicit\nnever-sync; a non-empty string is the sync target. `None` must route to `legacy_default`.\nRuntime-confirmed: `resolve_project({\"bridge_project\": None}, ld=\"LEG\")` → `None`\n(vs. explicit `\"LEG\"` → `\"LEG\"`); the outbound create gate (`outbound_differ.py:584`)\n`if not target: return` then drops the create. Confirmed original (not regression) via\n`git blame a22e6f3642`.\n\n## Fix plan\n\nRewrite `resolve_project` to honor the tri-state explicitly (and update its docstring to\ndocument the present-but-null `None` sentinel):\n\n    value = ticket.get(\"bridge_project\")\n    if value is None:      # absent key OR the None absent/legacy sentinel\n        return mapping.legacy_default or None\n    if value == \"\":        # explicit never-sync\n        return None\n    return value\n\n## Blast radius / caller-dependency sweep (gate CLEARED)\n\nSingle production caller: `outbound_differ.py:584` — the malfunctioning create gate itself,\nwhich expects the contract-correct target. No existing test pins `None`->None; all existing\ntests (`{}`->legacy_default, `\"\"`->None, empty-legacy->None) stay green. The only behavior change\nis the previously-untested `{\"bridge_project\": None}` case, changing toward the cef7 contract.\nThe outbound create is double-guarded — it fires only when the mapping is seeded AND\n`legacy_default` is both set and a key in the mapping — i.e. exactly the designed cef7 legacy\nmigration. No behavioral dependency on the buggy path found; gate clears without escalation.\n\n## Testing\n\n- Held-out RED unit test added to `tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_projects_store_heldout.py`,\n  verified RED before the fix and GREEN after; teeth proven by a defect-seeded mutation that\n  returns it to RED. Proof command:\n  `pytest tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_projects_store_heldout.py -q`.\n- Full projects-store + ensure-mapping suites stay green:\n  `pytest tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_projects_store_happy.py tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_projects_store_heldout.py tests/integration/test_ensure_project_mapping.py -q`.\n- Live DC rehearsal proven end-to-end in CI via the `Live External Integration` workflow:\n  `pytest tests/external/live_jira_dc/test_multi_project_rehearsal.py` with `REBAR_RUN_EXTERNAL=1`.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] Held-out RED unit test `resolve_project({\"bridge_project\": None}, ld=X) == X` seen RED\n      before the fix and GREEN after, teeth verified by defect-seeded mutation\n      (`pytest tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_projects_store_heldout.py -q`).\n- [ ] All existing `tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_projects_store_*.py` and\n      `tests/integration/test_ensure_project_mapping.py` stay green (command above).\n- [ ] Scenario 4 strengthened with a meaningful `{legacy} <= _planned_projects(preview)`\n      assertion, replacing the vacuous empty-plan `_assert_scope`.\n- [ ] A successful LIVE DC rehearsal run of `test_multi_project_rehearsal.py` (all scenarios\n      incl. scenario 4) passing in the CI `Live External Integration` workflow — proven\n      end-to-end, not merely built.\n- [ ] Landed through Gerrit at `LLM-Review +1` AND `Verified +1`."}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1786786622206459001,"uuid":"d15d6188-5bf4-4b7d-bfa9-0c953bf2ce36"}